{"action_id":null,"arguments":[],"assumptions":[{"assumption_id":"node.4e6a162c35678e9ddf17ad8e.a0","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"The assessment concerns one identified material change to an SFC-authorised fund’s investment objective, policy or restriction.","status":"PROVISIONAL"},{"assumption_id":"node.4e6a162c35678e9ddf17ad8e.a1","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"Product-feature and local-policy tests concern the proposed change, including features it introduces or alters, rather than an unrelated feature of the fund.","status":"PROVISIONAL"},{"assumption_id":"node.4e6a162c35678e9ddf17ad8e.a2","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"An application received before 28 November 2025 and still unapproved or unauthorised at the transition remains in the existing process; it is not treated as eligible to bypass that process through the new removal measure.","status":"PROVISIONAL"},{"assumption_id":"node.4e6a162c35678e9ddf17ad8e.a3","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"Failure to qualify for this removal does not, by itself, establish an independently applicable prior-approval obligation.","status":"PROVISIONAL"}],"bundle_hash":"5874936c74418d89b087db7f12194a7b2cb15c2c137438a9d5e53c2beb513c94","candidate_id":"candidate.49ad470311a340de95676a306d579c8a","controlled_language":"[TRUE_IS_SATISFIED] Within scope, true means the assessed change qualifies for this circular’s removal of prior SFC approval, subject to the stated transition interpretation. False means that removal is unavailable under this model, not that the change is prohibited or that an independent prior-approval obligation has been established. Outside scope no conclusion is supplied. Unknown inputs remain unknown. This result confers no legal approval.","disposition_reason":"Unreviewed interpretation proposal","family_ids":["exceptions"],"generation_phase":"BLIND_INITIAL","issue_ids":["issue.22b2fc41b73047ce992c0572566d997e","issue.dd190e6937de416092f320f6a67a1072","issue.5acd7e4d0a434817b330649a3ead274e","issue.b9de199e10e64582a1892222fe296764"],"parent_id":null,"probability_of_legal_correctness":null,"revision_reason":"Eligibility for removal of prior approval depends on both the change’s substantive components and the procedural history of its application. A single fund-level Boolean would hide change-specific exceptions and the pending-application transition. Removal also leaves post-vetting distinct from prior approval.","run_id":"run.57127ace1fc14bbe97f783a02f719446","scheduling_priority":0,"schema_version":"interpretation.v1","score_purpose":"INVESTIGATION_PRIORITY_ONLY","source_packet_hash":"6c557525c251e4c0794c0061ba5b7f7fec9be45d9495dd1ca07063f018b43c06","source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u10.1809","d97b56331f41a.u12.2069","d97b56331f41a.u17.2556","d97b56331f41a.u5.840","d97b56331f41a.u9.1696"],"status":"ACTIVE","subject_unit":"Eligibility of a material UCITS investment change for removal of prior SFC approval"}